; range_end_overflow: RANGE's exclusive bound is range-checked, not wrapped.
;
; start = 2^63 - 2, count = 3, so end = 2^63 + 1 is not representable. A
; VM that computes it with `wrapping_add` gets 2^63 + 1 mod 2^64 =
; -(2^63 - 1), which is less than `current`, so the loop runs exactly one
; iteration; one that computes in unbounded integers runs three. Different
; register contents, and different step counts -- and step count is
; metering on a chain that prices per step.
;
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md ranges its overflow rule over every i64 operation the VM
; performs on a program's behalf. Loop control is not carved out of it.

PUSH 9223372036854775806   ; start
PUSH 3                     ; count
RANGE
LIDX r0
NEXT
HALT
